e regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed; I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, which completed. Post-rollback status: version v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error_rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure before re-attempting the v2.3.1 release."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident creation timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created, so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Kk82jUafMUu2SRZnr1TVce", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Since v2.3.0 had been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollout:** The first attempt halted with an orchestrator partial failure after us-east, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Current status:** v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy=true, error rate 0.002 (down from 0.18).\n- **Incident:** The first incident call timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already created with the full summary, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and why the orchestrator halted the rollout partway through. Don't re-release v2.3.1 until both are understood.", "type": "text"}]}]}